<title>FRANCE: Thomson EGM on December 6-Arthuis.</title>
<headline>Thomson EGM on December 6-Arthuis.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis told parliament on Wednesday that an extraordinary shareholders' meeting of state-owned Thomson would be held on December 6 to decide on an increase of the share capital.</p>
<p>Thomson, which owns 100 percent of consumer electronics group Thomson Multimedia and 58 percent of defence electronics group Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Arthuis reaffirmed to parliament during question time that he had &quot;no intention of coming back&quot; on the government's decision to sell Thomson to Lagardere Groupe.</p>
<p>At the end of 1995, the state had a 75.89 percent direct stake in Thomson SA while state-owned telecommunications group France Telecom has a 19.90 percent stake.</p>
<p>The Caisse des Depots et Consignations (CDC) state bank and some other banks have a total 4.21 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
